        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_014owyDLH4FjEovmSpsMKFTj",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022pages/concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: Centralizing resource initialization and scope-management decisions at the Hub\u0027s startup to eliminate scattered environment configuration throughout the codebase.\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - tech/dotnet\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: Both credential-scoping and runtime-paths explicitly describe a single centralized place where decisions are made at startup, avoiding scattered logic across the codebase. The architectural principle is the same in both, and the pages jointly articulate a unified strategy.\\nreview_date: 2025-07-14\\n---\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] both embody the same architectural principle: making critical resource-binding decisions at a single point during Hub startup, then distributing the results downstream as immutable resolved values.\\n\\n**Credential Scoping** centralizes the decision of *who can see secrets*: a local secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from \u0060.env\u0060 once at startup and injects it only into spawned child processes\u0027 environments (Ingest and Query agents), never into the Hub\u0027s own environment. This prevents scattered, implicit environment-inheritance bugs where any part of the Hub might accidentally expose the credential.\\n\\n**Runtime Path Configuration** centralizes the decision of *where files live*: a single path resolver reads configuration at startup, validates all required locations exist, auto-creates missing writable directories, and reports the effective paths and their sources. This prevents scattered file-path logic across the codebase where different modules might try to locate the same resource in different ways.\\n\\nBoth decisions follow the same pattern:\\n1. A single, well-defined initialization point at Hub startup\\n2. A validated, centralized decision that reads configuration and applies policy\\n3. Immutable, already-resolved results distributed downstream\\n4. Prevention of scattered, ad-hoc rediscovery or retry logic in different parts of the codebase\\n\\nThis pattern reduces attack surface for credentials (they never inhabit the Hub\u0027s own environment) and reduces operational confusion for paths (all paths are known and reported at startup, not rediscovered at first use). Adding a new credential or a new runtime location means extending the single resolver, not patching logic throughout the system.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
